# License boundaries

First-party software in `src/`, `examples/`, `tests/`, `scripts/` and the
viewer code in `demo/` uses the existing [MIT license](LICENSE-CODE).
First-party prose and original analysis figures/tables use the existing
[CC BY 4.0 terms](LICENSE-DOCUMENTATION). External data and third-party software retain their separate rights.

NASA/TESS/MAST observations, NASA Exoplanet Archive factual records, third-party
software, literature, mission identifiers and trademarks are not relicensed.
The saved-record viewer contains mixed-origin factual records and a small
display sample derived from mission observations. Retain their provenance
and acknowledgments. See [rights scope](THIRD_PARTY_AND_DATA_RIGHTS.md) and
[file coverage](provenance/license_coverage.csv).

Archived July files retain their recorded notices and historical coverage map.
The RC1/RC2 labels inside preserved notices are historical, not the version of
the current software version.
